{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785994621689168001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"crass-queue-cup","assignee":"","author":"Claude","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":4},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1783148935961551324,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[],"description":"## Why\n\nThe MCP `run_workflow` docstring in `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py` claims the run\n\"executes in the background so it survives client timeouts\" and \"Run-state\npersists durably ... (resumable on crash)\". The implementation is a\n`threading.Thread(target=_bg, daemon=True)` (around `_mcp_writes.py:297`). A\ndaemon thread does NOT survive process exit, and there is no reaper or\n`workflow resume` entrypoint that re-drives an orphaned run — so if the MCP host\nexits, the run is stranded at `running` forever. The docstring oversells a\ndurability guarantee the code does not provide. Since MCP tools are\nmodel-controlled, that inaccuracy can mislead an agent into relying on\nnon-existent crash-durability.\n\n## What\n\nCorrect the honesty of the durability wording (documentation only — the durable\nrunner itself is explicitly OUT of scope):\n\n- Rewrite the `run_workflow` docstring to state true semantics: the background\n  work runs on a **daemon thread that does not survive MCP-process exit**; there\n  is **no automatic reaper**; step records are persisted with idempotency keys so\n  a run **can be resumed only if re-invoked**, but nothing auto-resumes it.\n- Align any adjacent claims that imply automatic crash-resumption\n  (e.g. `llm/workflow/runs.py` \"durable; resumable\" phrasing) so they describe\n  the persistence substrate, not an automatic guarantee.\n\n## Files\n\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py` (the `run_workflow` docstring)\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/runs.py` (align wording if it overstates)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The `run_workflow` docstring no longer implies the daemon thread survives\n  process exit or that runs auto-resume after a crash.\n- [ ] It accurately states: daemon thread, no reaper, resume requires\n  re-invocation, step records are idempotent.\n- [ ] Any adjacent \"resumable on crash\" wording is aligned to describe the\n  persistence substrate, not an automatic guarantee.\n- [ ] No runtime/behavior change; `make lint` stays green.","env_id":"58e9f32e-f999-436d-9c1a-5d0eef5c9903","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py","reason":"fix docstring"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/runs.py","reason":"align wording"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","b02d-10bc-07ee-49e7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"b02d-10bc-07ee-49e7","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"e110-8911-af25-46f0","ticket_type":"task","title":"Fix run_workflow durability docstring to state true crash semantics","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6804425b-ab92-401b-94b3-b59b4afe5b85","375aecda-3e64-4444-92d3-89c1dfd49a1e","51b75ec8-4b25-4088-8cdd-fa2d10ee6646","9e9d6ab7-989c-457d-8619-e4a25a153a39","aee18244-cb31-4cb5-8172-ca5b09f3d5a1"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785994621689168001,"uuid":"0a23736e-c262-408b-8edf-a4dd1d018e98"}